  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Government Capacities on Migration Management and Supporting the Regularization of Venezuelan Refugees and Migrants in the Latin America and Caribbean Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project implemented in Latin America &amp; Caribbean (LAC) and particularly in Panama and Colombia consists in supporting the Regularization and Socio-Economic Integration of Venezuelan refugees and migrants (VRMs) Regional through the design and development of regularization toolkit, and the trainings to enhance the capacities of host governments, private sector and Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) in the design, implementation, and dissemination of regularization mechanisms in the LAC region; developing a guide on regularization for Venezuelan NGOs to be used by CSOs to provide technical advice to VRMs on regularization processes; reinforcing protection capacities at Panama&#x2019;s National Ombudsperson&#x2019;s Office for migrants with a Human Rights-based approach; providing technical assistance on Colombia&#x2019;s national regularization program to public and private entities to promote social inclusion; combating different forms of intolerance including Xenophobia; improving migration and border management capacity building for Panama&#x2019;s government officials on migration management, and for Colombia on Integrated Border Management, Humanitarian Border Management; supporting the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) carried out in Panama to increase data collection; and promoting Regular Migration Pathways vs. Irregular Pathways Awareness raising campaign, in Panama, on risks of Dari&#xe9;n Gap Crossings.</narrative>
  </description>
